{
  "description": "Typed failure next to the error text (Android ExchangeFailure.kt / iOS ExchangeFailure.swift). classify: RefreshReportLogic.classify(failure, text) - a failure kind that decides (timeout, offline, ssl, httpStatus, rateLimited, unknownInstrument) wins over the text; parse, message, other and no failure (null, e.g. stored error strings) fall back to the keyword match on the text. httpStatus: code from the kind, else from the text. confirmedBySingle: NotTraded.confirmedBySingle(gotPrice, text, failure) - the kind decides where it can; other (internal error without a clear type) never confirms; parse and exchange fall back to the text rules, but a blank text only confirms without a kind (null). The single ticker reports an answer without a valid price (missing, 0, NaN, infinite) as parse with 'Parsed ticker has no data'. regionBlocked: RefreshReportLogic.isRegionBlocked(text) - HTTP 451 in the stored text is the region block (own message instead of «not reachable», no retry hint). accessDenied: RefreshReportLogic.isAccessDenied(text) - HTTP 403 in the stored text without a rate-limit text is a refused access (own message «denied access» instead of «not reachable», no retry hint). pairListAborts: pairListCallAborts(call, allRequired, failure) - a pair list loaded in several requests (BitFlyer, Deribit) aborts as a whole (the stored list stays) when the failing request is the first, every request is required, or the failure is transient (timeout, offline, ssl, rate limit, HTTP 408 or 5xx); a lasting failure of a later request (4xx, unreadable) skips that part. pairListAttempt: remembersPairListAttempt(failure) - the portfolio remembers a pair-list load (hours of rest) only after a result: loaded (null) or a lasting answer; a transient failure is retried on the next refresh.",
